====================================================================================================================================
PARTISAN vs NEUTRAL — the same decisions, contested by different challengers
====================================================================================================================================
NEUTRAL   rerule-recontest            records/experiments/rerule/recontest/index.jsonl
PARTISAN  partisan-pilot-advocate     outputs/experiments/partisan-pilot-advocate/index.jsonl
PARTISAN  partisan-pilot-assigned     outputs/experiments/partisan-pilot-assigned/index.jsonl
PARTISAN  partisan-pilot-auditor      outputs/experiments/partisan-pilot-auditor/index.jsonl

WHAT THIS COMPARISON MEANS
------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Under the partisan variant the challenger is ASSIGNED the answer the decision
went against and argues the decision was mistaken; it may still report finding
no grounds. So 'detection' here reads 'could an advocate find grounds', and
false alarms on correct decisions are high BY CONSTRUCTION. What the ablation
measures at raised n is the JUDGE (does it overturn genuine-on-wrong more than
genuine-on-correct), the GRADER (valid-objection rate), the phantom rate under
advocacy, and how often an advocate declines when the record supports the
decision. The neutral column is the design's primary measurement; the raise
rates in the two columns are different quantities and must not be pooled.

Decisions, labels and conditions are IDENTICAL across the columns by
construction — every run reads the sweep's decisions — and this is asserted
cell by cell below. Everything downstream of the challenger is what differs.

