====================================================================================================================================
(f) THE GRADER — did the objection name the flaw the dataset annotates?
====================================================================================================================================
The grade stage's own gate (run_stage_grade) is: the stance is `contests` AND
the item is gold-flawed with an annotation AND the DECISION WAS INCORRECT —
`P(valid objection | initially incorrect)`, so an objection to a decision that
was right is a false alarm whose validity is undefined by design and is never
graded. `gradable & contested & wrong` below is that gate as far as the index
can express it (annotation_quality is not an index column, so a cell whose
annotation records nothing to grade against shows up as eligible-but-ungraded).
n is small and is printed with every rate. The index columns are
`identified_flaw`, `characterises_the_flaw` and `grade_valid` (build_index emits
no `grade_identified`).

